Portions of zsh/modules/tools.zsh, zsh/modules/remote.zsh and install.sh are
adapted from GCR (https://github.com/gaojunbin/GCR) by Junbin Gao, released
under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Adapted ideas and command names include: trash-based rm (del / delf /
empty_trash), git shortcuts (gita, gitaa, gitb, gitc, gitch, gitl, gitr,
gitpl, gitps, gitst), sz, pid, pathadd, mychmod / mychown, listen (SSH port
forwarding), upload / download (trzsz), dockeradd, and the oh-my-zsh +
powerlevel10k + plugin setup.

Changes made: the code was rewritten for macOS and Linux portability; the
interactive menus became commands that also accept arguments; site-specific
features (VPN/proxy tools, self-hosted server apps, HPC-cluster helpers,
auto-update from the upstream repo) were removed; gitps pushes the current
branch instead of master; the trash follows each OS's own trash location.
